<title>ITALY: Bari airport cargo traffic down 42.5pct in Jan 97.</title>
<headline>Bari airport cargo traffic down 42.5pct in Jan 97.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1997-02-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Cargo traffic handled at Bari Palese airport in Italy totalled 65.6 tonnes in January 1997, a decline of 42.5 percent against the same period 1995, the airport's managing company, SEAP said.</p>
<p>						Pct change</p>
<p>						against Jan 96</p>
<p> Cargo imports	    34.9	  down 58.8pct</p>
<p> Cargo exports	    30.6	  up    5.2pct</p>
<p> Total cargo		65.6	  down 42.5</p>
<p> Total mail		106.3	  down 39.8</p>
<p> Total passengers     69,325	  up   27.6</p>
<p>- Reuters Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44 171 542 7706 Fax:5017</p>
</text>
